WEBVTT


00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.320
Getting started to knit quickly is
a snap using Garment Designer.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.910
How many times have you wanted to make a quick
sweater for an upcoming baby shower?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:16.830
You wanted something quick and easy and you wanted to
take time to embellish the garment and not spend

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.110
a whole lot of time in front of the
compute. With Garment Designer

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.440
you can do this in just a few steps.

00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:29.384
We're going to create this cardigan simple
baby cardigan in less than 10 steps.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:30.335
Let's get started.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.180
When you start a new pattern, the first thing you'll
notice is that there's a default garment on the

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.150
screen. We will use this as
our starting point.

00:00:39.519 --> 00:00:46.230
Also, you'll see lots of lines. The green lines represent
the sloper which actually represents the

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:50.170
body and the black line
is the actual pattern.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.830
So we are showing that we have some breathing room, some
ease in this garment. To make things simpler.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:00.170
Let's go ahead and turn the sloper
off we'll click >display and >show pattern.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.150
And that makes things a whole
lot easier to see.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.270
Now we're going to be designing
a cardigan.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.880
Let's set up our pieces
>display and >pieces.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.040
Our garment pieces are front.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:20.580
We both need both a right and a left, but they're not
going to be joined because it's a cardigan, they

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.110
will be independent.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:25.720
We need a right and a left back,
but we want those joined.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:27.350
We want one single back.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.290
Our Sleeve has a front and a back
but we also want it joined.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.350
There's no seam down that sleeve.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.740
We're only going to work with one sleeve.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.660
We don't need both of them on the screen.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:39.270
Click.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.000
OK and there we go.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.410
Looks like we're getting close here.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:49.770
Now before we forget let's enter our gauge.
We'll go to >options >units and gauge.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.680
We've got some choices here.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.740
I'm going to use stitches
and rows per inch.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.230
Five and seven and click, OK.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.490
The next thing we need to set up on
our pattern is a size.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:05.840
We're going to be making a child sweater.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.940
I don't want to do an infant's let's
make it a toddler sweater.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:13.770
So that baby has something to grow
into. We can change the size here.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.280
We'll make it a 2 toddlers.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:22.240
And one thing I do notice is that this is
a set in sleeve now for baby sweaters.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.500
I don't need to be bothered.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.550
This is supposed to be quick and easy.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.400
Let's make this just a straight
drop shoulder sleeve.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.400
Again, very little shaping
quick and easy.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:39.050
Another thing that I notice is there is a
sloped shoulder. For children's clothing

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.050
you really don't need to
slope that shoulder.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.950
It's just a little more shaping
while you're knitting. Again

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:51.480
we want this thing to be fast. Change it from
sloped to straight and there we are.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.070
We've got the basics of our sweater.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.300
Believe it or not.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.030
We're ready to start knitting.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:07.530
I'd like to save this garment we'll >file and >save
as and we'll call it BABY and click on Save.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.480
The next thing we want to do is see the
pattern. Where are my instructions?

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:17.830
I've got some nice pretty pictures on the screen.
will click >generate >shaping instructions and

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.430
voila.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.360
There's our shaping instructions.

00:03:20.945 --> 00:03:27.405
Click >file and >print these will print out for you. Take
them over to your knitting machine and you are

00:03:27.405 --> 00:03:33.365
ready to go. Very few steps, a couple of
minutes and you're ready to go.

00:03:34.105 --> 00:03:34.195
Now

00:03:34.225 --> 00:03:40.215
If you're not used to the shaping instructions in
Garment Designer they're little bit different, but

00:03:40.215 --> 00:03:46.185
the first time you use them you will fall in love with
them. You follow the instructions from the bottom

00:03:46.365 --> 00:03:46.715
up.

00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:48.935
So this is our right front.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.870
We're going to cast on 31 stitches.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.350
We're going to knit to
row 81. And it row 81

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.420
we're going to start shaping
our neckline.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.610
We're going to take off 2 stitches which
will leave us 29. The next row

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.850
we're going to be taking off 2 stitches
on the right hand side.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:16.810
Take us down to 27 all the way up to Row
90 where our last shaping takes place.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:21.810
Row 95 we're all done and
will bind off 21.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:29.630
So the next time you want a really quick sweater. Turn
to Garment Designer and you'll be knitting in no

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:29.970
time.